update public.questions set solution = $F$The rate is $480 \div 12 = 40$ pages per minute. $1$ hour $30$ minutes is $90$ minutes, so $40 \times 90 = 3600$ pages.$F$ where id = 'ai_1792374083695_f1zz4l';
update public.questions set solution = $F$$5$ km $= 500\,000$ cm. On Map A: $500\,000 \div 100\,000 = 5$ cm. On Map B: $500\,000 \div 50\,000 = 10$ cm.$F$ where id = 'ai_1792374106445_uuxbxf';
update public.questions set solution = $F$Each centimetre on the map is $50\,000$ real centimetres: $4 \times 50\,000 = 200\,000$ cm $= 2000$ m $= 2$ km.$F$ where id = 'ai_1792374106445_y1yvu0';
update public.questions set solution = $F$Average speed $=$ total distance $\div$ total time. Total distance $= 180 + 140 = 320$ km and total time $= 4$ hours, so $320 \div 4 = 80$ km/h.$F$ where id = 'ai_1792374143415_qapla3';
update public.questions set solution = $F$$90$ km/h means $90\,000$ m in $3600$ seconds: $90\,000 \div 3600 = 25$ m/s.$F$ where id = 'ai_1792374161527_yewo43';
update public.questions set solution = $F$Substitute $a = 4$ and $b = 3$: $2 \times 4^2 + 3 \times 3 - 5 = 2 \times 16 + 9 - 5 = 32 + 9 - 5 = 36$.$F$ where id = 'ai_1792374180041_2yae9d';
update public.questions set solution = $F$Substitute $l = 8$ and $w = 5$: $P = 2(8) + 2(5) = 16 + 10 = 26$ cm.$F$ where id = 'ai_1792374180042_8p9ium';
update public.questions set solution = $F$Subtract $3x$ from both sides: $4x - 4 = 12$. Add $4$ to both sides: $4x = 16$. Divide by $4$: $x = 4$. Check: $7(4) - 4 = 24$ and $3(4) + 12 = 24$ ✓$F$ where id = 'ai_1792374258196_6308xf';
update public.questions set solution = $F$Subtract $4x$ from both sides: $5x + 3 = 23$. Subtract $3$: $5x = 20$. Divide by $5$: $x = 4$. Check: $9(4) + 3 = 39$ and $4(4) + 23 = 39$ ✓$F$ where id = 'ai_1792374258196_i0cdnf';
update public.questions set solution = $F$Subtract $x$ from both sides: $2x + 5 = 13$. Subtract $5$: $2x = 8$. Divide by $2$: $x = 4$. Check: $3(4) + 5 = 17$ and $4 + 13 = 17$ ✓$F$ where id = 'ai_1792374258196_ksn326';
update public.questions set solution = $F$Angles on a straight line add to $180°$: $(3x + 15) + (2x + 25) = 180$, so $5x + 40 = 180$, $5x = 140$ and $x = 28$.$F$ where id = 'ai_1792374414866_23pqrh';
update public.questions set solution = $F$Angles around a point add to $360°$. The four known angles add to $72 + 68 + 85 + 79 = 304°$, so the fifth is $360 - 304 = 56°$.$F$ where id = 'ai_1792374414866_5y246d';
update public.questions set solution = $F$Vertically opposite angles are equal, so the angle opposite $124°$ is also $124°$. Angles on a straight line add to $180°$, so each of the other two is $180 - 124 = 56°$. The other three angles are $124°$, $56°$ and $56°$.$F$ where id = 'ai_1792374414866_byo42w';
update public.questions set solution = $F$The scale factor is $12 \div 8 = 1.5$. Every length, including the perimeter, is multiplied by $1.5$: $48 \times 1.5 = 72$ cm.$F$ where id = 'ai_1792374449802_fpvo4t';
update public.questions set solution = $F$Area of a trapezium $= \frac{1}{2}(a + b)h = \frac{1}{2}(7 + 9) \times 4 = \frac{1}{2} \times 16 \times 4 = 32$ cm$^2$.$F$ where id = 'ai_1792374523624_4j6te3';
update public.questions set solution = $F$Rectangle: $8 \times 5 = 40$ cm$^2$. Square: $5 \times 5 = 25$ cm$^2$. Total: $40 + 25 = 65$ cm$^2$.$F$ where id = 'ai_1792374566708_dw5snm';
update public.questions set solution = $F$The ladder is the hypotenuse. Height$^2 = 4^2 - 3^2 = 16 - 9 = 7$, so the height is $\sqrt{7}$ m (about $2.6$ m).$F$ where id = 'ai_1792374651387_hkbex5';
update public.questions set solution = $F$Volume of material $=$ outer cylinder $-$ inner cylinder $= \pi(5^2 - 3^2) \times 20 = 3.14 \times 16 \times 20 = 1004.8$ cm$^3$, which is about $1005$ cm$^3$.$F$ where id = 'ai_1792374689361_mfx3kd';
update public.questions set solution = $F$Convert everything to millilitres: $1.5$ L $= 1500$ mL and $0.7$ L $= 700$ mL. Total: $1500 + 800 + 700 = 3000$ mL.$F$ where id = 'ai_1792374733199_1kavhu';
update public.questions set solution = $F$Losing $60$ litres at $0.5$ litres per hour takes $60 \div 0.5 = 120$ hours, and $120 \div 24 = 5$ days.$F$ where id = 'ai_1792374733199_8srjfq';
